        troubleshooting: `If the command is not recognised, the NetAdapter module is missing, which happens on very old Windows versions (before Windows 8 and Server 2012). If an adapter is not listed, try -IncludeHidden. A Status of Disabled means someone turned it off (Enable-NetAdapter turns it on again; run it in an elevated window); Disconnected means no cable or network is detected; Not Present means the hardware is gone. On a Server Core machine all of this works in the same way, which is why this cmdlet is the first step before assigning a static IP.`,
